      15: [{ week: 15, keyword: "review", question: "What kind of number is $3.50 with a dot in it?", options: ["A fraction B) A bar C) A decimal D) A graph"], answer: "C", explanation: "", passage: "In math class, we learn how to calculate money. Money usually has a dot, so it is a decimal number, like $3.50. If you buy a toy, you subtract the money from your wallet. If you get pocket money, you add it to your total." }],
